\ wallet.fam — the wallet (docs/GUI_WALLET.md, phase 1), for wm's wallet
\ window: wm runs it as the session's user in the user's home, on pipes,
\ and it speaks the wallet's messages (docs/GUI_WALLET.md, The wallet's
\ messages): a JSON object a line each way, the first line wm's unlock
\ with the session's password, then each request answered by its op with
\ its id echoed.  It reads compact JSON (as JSON.stringify writes it).  It
\ ends when its input does.
\
\ Its records are a tree in the user's home, .wallet (mode 700), as
\ tabminer's wallet keeps an LMDB environment: "secret" the phrase's
\ entropy and its BIP39 seed, sealed under the password as tabminer seals
\ them (1, the rounds, a salt, a nonce, then ChaCha20-Poly1305 of the 80
\ bytes with the 33 before as associated data, the key the first 32
\ bytes of PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512 of the password and "tabminer wallet" ||
\ salt); "address" the address counter (8 bytes; a new or restored
\ wallet's starts at a random 60-bit number: old addresses are never
\ used again, docs/PRIVACY.md); "scan" 1 while a restore waits for its
\ first scan.  The password is the session's: wm's, as typed at logging
\ in.
\
\ The node is its API on 127.0.0.1:3738, without the token (reads are
\ open).  The wallet's outputs are found by reading the whole unspent set
\ (/v1/outputs, a thousand a request) and checking each memo's tag: one
\ of this wallet's has its key derived and its commitment checked before
\ it is recorded; one once in the set and no longer there was spent.  The
\ set is read again whenever the tip moves (the node asked every 4 s
\ while no request comes), and the tip told (an event); a reorganization
\ needs nothing more.  Reading block by block can come later, when the
\ set is large.
\
\ Built so far (step 2 of 4): unlock, create, restore, phrase, receive,
\ overview, scan; the tip told.  The rest are refused as not yet built.
\ uses: crypto/sha512.fam crypto/sha256.fam crypto/bip39.fam crypto/chacha.fam crypto/keccak.fam crypto/dilithium.fam crypto/kyber.fam
\ uses: node/arith.fam node/poseidon2.fam node/difficulty.fam node/pow.fam node/state.fam node/xmss.fam node/xsign.fam node/wkeys.fam node/wslate.fam node/wproof.fam node/wname.fam node/wmsg.fam node/dns.fam node/wnet.fam
\ memory: 6144
: ibuf variable ;  : icnt variable ;  : obuf variable ;  : opos variable ;
: idb variable ;  : opb variable ;  : unl variable ;  : jr variable ;
: lp variable ;  : le variable ;

\ jo ( s -- )  s added to the line being written, each ' a double quote
\ (fam's strings hold none); jraw ( s -- ) s as it is; jend the line
\ written, a newline after it.
: jo
opos @ swap
begin dup c@ ?dup while dup 27 lit = if drop 22 lit then 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat
drop opos ! ;
: jraw  opos @ swap scpy opos ! ;
: jend  A lit opos @ c!  1 lit obuf @ opos @ obuf @ - 1 lit + write drop  obuf @ opos ! ;

\ jfm ( a key -- flag )  key (' for a double quote) at a.
\ jfind ( line key -- a | 0 )  just past the first key in the line.
: jfm
begin dup c@ if over c@ over c@ dup 27 lit = if drop 22 lit then = else 0 lit then while
	1 lit + swap 1 lit + swap
repeat
nip c@ 0= ;
: jfind
0 lit jr !  swap
begin dup c@ jr @ 0= and while
	2dup swap jfm if dup 2 lit pick strlen + jr ! then
	1 lit +
repeat 2drop jr @ ;

\ getid ( line -- )  the request's id at idb as sent (up to a comma or a
\ brace), or null; getop ( line -- ) its op at opb (31 bytes at most), or
\ empty.
: getid
idb @ swap "'id':" jfind ?dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 2C lit <> over 7D lit <> and and while dup c@ 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat drop
else "null" scpy then
0 lit swap c! ;
: getop
opb @ swap "'op':'" jfind ?dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 22 lit <> and  2 lit pick opb @ - 1F lit u< and while
		dup c@ 2 lit pick c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat drop
then
0 lit swap c! ;

\ jstr ( line key dst max -- flag )  the string after key (as "'words':'")
\ at dst, its escapes undone (\" \\ \/ \n \t \r \b \f, \u00XX), NUL-ended,
\ max - 1 bytes at most; whether the key was there and the string fit.
: jsd variable ;  : jsm variable ;  : jsok variable ;
: jhx  dup 3A lit u< if 30 lit - else 20 lit or 57 lit - then F lit and ;   \ ( c -- n )
: jsput  jsm @ 1 lit u> if jsd @ c!  jsd @ 1 lit + jsd !  jsm @ 1 lit - jsm ! else drop 0 lit jsok ! then ;
: jstr
jsm !  jsd !  jfind dup jsok !
dup if
	begin dup c@ dup 22 lit <> and while
		dup c@ 5C lit = if
			1 lit +  dup c@
			dup 6E lit = if drop A lit else dup 74 lit = if drop 9 lit else dup 72 lit = if drop D lit else
			dup 62 lit = if drop 8 lit else dup 66 lit = if drop C lit else
			dup 75 lit = if drop dup 3 lit + c@ jhx 4 lit lshift over 4 lit + c@ jhx or  swap 4 lit + swap then
			then then then then then
			jsput
		else dup c@ jsput then
		1 lit +
	repeat
	c@ 0= if 0 lit jsok ! then
else drop then
0 lit jsd @ c!  jsok @ 0= 0= ;

\ jok  an answer begun: its id, ok; jerr ( s -- ) an error answered.
: jok  "{'id':" jo idb @ jraw ",'ok':true" jo ;
\ jsafe ( s -- )  text from elsewhere made safe in an answer: its quotes and
\ backslashes (jo would close the string on them) turned to backticks, its
\ control bytes to spaces.
: jsafe
begin dup c@ while
	dup c@ dup 27 lit = over 22 lit = or swap 5C lit = or if 60 lit over c! then
	dup c@ 20 lit u< if 20 lit over c! then
	1 lit +
repeat drop ;
: jerr  "{'id':" jo idb @ jraw ",'ok':false,'error':'" jo jo "'}" jo jend ;
: op?  opb @ swap streq ;                                    \ ( s -- flag )

\ ── The records ──

: wfd variable ;  : pw variable ;  : have variable ;  : rec variable ;  : plain variable ;  : wkey variable ;
: salt2 variable ;  : wphr variable ;  : wseed variable ;  : wtmp variable ;  : wcnt variable ;
: wpk variable ;  : wsk variable ;  : waddr variable ;  : wf1 variable ;  : wf2 variable ;
:M ROUNDS 4E20 lit ;                         \ the password's PBKDF2 rounds (fam's: about 1.4 s)

\ wrand ( dst n -- )  n bytes from /dev/random.
: wrf variable ;  : wrd variable ;  : wrn variable ;
: wrand
wrn !  wrd !  "/dev/random" 0 lit open wrf !
begin wrn @ while
	wrf @ wrd @ wrn @ read  dup 0 lit > if dup wrd @ + wrd !  wrn @ swap - wrn ! else drop then
repeat
wrf @ close drop ;
\ wopen ( create? -- flag )  the tree open (made, mode 700, if asked).
: wopen
wfd @ 0< 0= if drop -1 lit else
	".wallet" TREE 2 lit or rot if CREATE or then open dup wfd !
	0< 0= dup if ".wallet" 1C0 lit chmod drop then
then ;
\ wget ( key buf n -- vlen | <0 )  one record, read in a snapshot.
\ wbeg  the writer's transaction begun; wset ( key value n -- ) a record
\ in it; wend ( -- ok ) it committed, all its records or none.
: wgk variable ;  : wtx variable ;
: wget  wf2 !  wf1 !  wgk !  wfd @ 0 lit txbegin  dup wgk @ dup strlen wf1 @ wf2 @ txget  swap txabort drop ;
: wbeg  wfd @ 1 lit txbegin wtx ! ;
: wset  wf2 !  wf1 !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ dup strlen wf1 @ wf2 @ txput drop ;
: wend  wtx @ txcommit 0= ;

\ wkdf ( pw rec -- )  wkey (32 bytes) = PBKDF2 of the password with the
\ record's rounds and "tabminer wallet" || its salt (16 bytes at 5).
: wkr variable ;  : wkp variable ;
: wkdf
wkr !  wkp !
salt2 @ "tabminer wallet" scpy  wkr @ 5 lit + swap 10 lit bcopy
wkp @ dup strlen salt2 @ 1F lit wkr @ 1 lit + le@ wtmp @ 40 lit pbkdf512
wtmp @ wkey @ 20 lit bcopy ;
\ wseal  rec (129 bytes) = plain (the entropy, the seed) sealed under pw:
\ 1, the rounds, a salt (16), a nonce (12), the 96 sealed bytes.
: wseal
1 lit rec @ c!  ROUNDS rec @ 1 lit + wkle!  rec @ 5 lit + 10 lit wrand  rec @ 15 lit + C lit wrand
pw @ rec @ wkdf
wkey @ rec @ 15 lit + rec @ 21 lit plain @ 50 lit rec @ 21 lit + aeseal ;
\ wunseal ( pw -- flag )  plain from the record, if the password is its.
: wunseal
"secret" rec @ 100 lit wget 81 lit =  rec @ c@ 1 lit = and
dup if
	drop rec @ wkdf
	wkey @ rec @ 15 lit + rec @ 21 lit rec @ 21 lit + 50 lit plain @ aeopen
else nip then ;

\ The address: the Dilithium key of the address counter, its id in text.
: waok variable ;
: waddr!
waok @ 0= if
	wcnt @ wtmp @ wkidsd  wtmp @ wpk @ wsk @ dilkey  wpk @ wtmp @ wkid  wtmp @ waddr @ wkaddr
	1 lit waok !
then ;
\ wrcnt  a new counter: 60 random bits.
: wrcnt
wcnt @ 8 lit wrand
wcnt @ @ 4 lit rshift  wcnt @ 4 lit + @ 1C lit lshift or
wcnt @ 4 lit + @ 4 lit rshift  wcnt @ 4 lit + !  wcnt @ ! ;
\ wmake ( scan? -- ok )  a wallet made from plain: the tree, its records
\ in one transaction; the master.
: wmake
1 lit wopen if
	wrcnt  wseal  0 lit waok !
	wbeg
	"secret" rec @ 81 lit wset
	1 lit wtmp @ c!  "format" wtmp @ 1 lit wset
	"address" wcnt @ 8 lit wset
	if 1 lit wtmp @ c!  "scan" wtmp @ 1 lit wset then
	wend
	dup if plain @ 10 lit + wkmast  1 lit have ! then
else drop 0 lit then ;
\ wload  an opened wallet's records: the counter, the master.
: wload  "address" wcnt @ 8 lit wget drop  plain @ 10 lit + wkmast  1 lit have !  0 lit waok ! ;

\ ── The node: its API (docs/NODE.md, The API), on 127.0.0.1:3738 ──

: hbuf variable ;  : hreq variable ;  : hs variable ;  : hn variable ;  : hres variable ;  : hpath variable ;
:M HMAX 40000 lit ;
: wcrlf  D lit over c!  1 lit +  A lit over c!  1 lit + ;      \ ( a -- a' )
\ hbody  hres = the body of the answer in hbuf (after the blank line).
: hbody
hn @ 3 lit - 0 lit do
	hres @ 0= if
		hbuf @ i + c@ D lit =  hbuf @ i + 1 lit + c@ A lit = and  hbuf @ i + 2 lit + c@ D lit = and
		if hbuf @ i + 4 lit + hres ! then
	then
loop ;
\ Numbers of 64 bits, as nlo and dhi.
: nlo variable ;  : nhi variable ;  : ndc variable ;  : nla variable ;  : nlb variable ;  : nca variable ;  : ncb variable ;
: nls variable ;  : nc1 variable ;  : nc2 variable ;  : nq0 variable ;  : nq1 variable ;  : nq2 variable ;  : nq3 variable ;
: ndn variable ;  : ntmp variable ;
\ d10+ ( d -- )  dlo:dhi times ten, plus d.
: d10+
ndc !
nlo @ 3 lit lshift nla !  nlo @ 1D lit rshift nca !
nlo @ 1 lit lshift nlb !  nlo @ 1F lit rshift ncb !
nla @ nlb @ + nls !  nls @ nla @ u< 1 lit and nc1 !
nls @ ndc @ + dup nls @ u< 1 lit and nc2 !  nlo !
nhi @ A lit * nca @ + ncb @ + nc1 @ + nc2 @ + nhi ! ;
\ jnum ( a -- a' )  the decimal digits at a into dlo:dhi; a' past them.
: jnum  0 lit nlo !  0 lit nhi !  begin dup c@ 30 lit - A lit u< while dup c@ 30 lit - d10+ 1 lit + repeat ;
\ dq16 ( r limb -- r' q )  one 16-bit step of dividing by ten.
: dq16  swap 10 lit lshift or  dup A lit /  tuck A lit * -  swap ;
\ du10 ( -- r )  dlo:dhi divided by ten; the remainder.
: du10
0 lit  nhi @ 10 lit rshift dq16 nq3 !  nhi @ FFFF lit and dq16 nq2 !
nlo @ 10 lit rshift dq16 nq1 !  nlo @ FFFF lit and dq16 nq0 !
nq3 @ 10 lit lshift nq2 @ or nhi !  nq1 @ 10 lit lshift nq0 @ or nlo ! ;
\ ddig ( lo hi n -- )  its decimal digits at dtmp, least first, n at
\ least; how many in dn.
: ddig
ndc !  nhi !  nlo !  0 lit ndn !
begin du10 30 lit + ntmp @ ndn @ + c!  ndn @ 1 lit + ndn !  nlo @ nhi @ or 0= ndn @ ndc @ u< 0= and until ;
\ jc ( c -- )  a byte added to the line being written.
: jc  opos @ c!  opos @ 1 lit + opos ! ;
\ wamt ( lo hi -- )  an amount in coins, its ten decimals, written.
: wamt
B lit ddig
ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ jc  ndn @ 1 lit - i - A lit = if 2E lit jc then loop ;
\ wdec ( lo hi -- )  a number in decimal, written.
: wdec  1 lit ddig  ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ jc loop ;
\ dstr ( lo hi dst -- dst' )  the same into a string.
: dstr  -rot 1 lit ddig  ndn @ 0 lit do ntmp @ ndn @ 1 lit - i - + c@ over c!  1 lit + loop  0 lit over c! ;
\ jhexb ( a dst n -- )  n bytes from 2n hex digits at a.
: jhexb  0 lit do over i 1 lit lshift + c@ jhx 4 lit lshift  2 lit pick i 1 lit lshift + 1 lit + c@ jhx or  over i + c! loop 2drop ;

\ hask ( method path body n -- body | 0 )  a request (a body of n bytes
\ unless n is 0) answered: its body, NUL-ended; the status in hcode (0:
\ the node not reached).
: hcode variable ;  : hmeth variable ;  : hbd variable ;  : hbn variable ;
: hask
hbn !  hbd !  hpath !  hmeth !  0 lit hn !  0 lit hres !  0 lit hcode !
2 lit socket hs !
hs @ 2 lit 7F000001 lit E9A lit net 0< 0= if
	hreq @ hmeth @ scpy " " scpy hpath @ scpy " HTTP/1.0" scpy wcrlf
	hbn @ if "Content-Length: " scpy hbn @ 0 lit rot dstr wcrlf then
	wcrlf hreq @ -
	hs @ hreq @ rot write drop
	hbn @ if hs @ hbd @ hbn @ write drop then
	begin hs @ hbuf @ hn @ + HMAX 1 lit - hn @ - read  dup 0 lit > while hn @ + hn ! repeat drop
	0 lit hbuf @ hn @ + c!
	hn @ C lit u< 0= if
		hbuf @ 9 lit + c@ 30 lit - 64 lit *  hbuf @ A lit + c@ 30 lit - A lit * +  hbuf @ B lit + c@ 30 lit - + hcode !
		hbody
	then
then
hs @ close drop  hres @ ;
\ hget ( path -- body | 0 )  a GET answered 200: its body.
: hget  "GET" swap 0 lit 0 lit hask  hcode @ C8 lit = and ;

\ ── Payments made: records "p" || the transaction's id (33 bytes), PREC
\ bytes each: +0 the amount, +8 the fee, +10 the commitment paid to, +30
\ the slate's id, +50 the sender (an address's id, or a secret's tag),
\ +70 1 if the secret is kept, +74 the secret, +94 where the output paid
\ to landed (8; all ones: not yet), +9C its height, +A0 the output (60
\ bytes: key hash, amount, memo); DC bytes in all.  The recipient's
\ receipt (its Dilithium key, 1,952 bytes; its signature, 3,309) beside
\ it in six parts ("q" || the id || the part's number, 896 bytes each but
\ the last: the store's values are 1 KiB at most), read back after the
\ record at +DC: all a proof of payment needs (docs/PROOFS.md) once the
\ output has landed. ──
:M PREC 1570 lit ;
:M PRECN DC lit ;
:M RPART 380 lit ;
: prec variable ;  : lnd variable ;  : nlnd variable ;

\ ── The outputs: records "o" || commitment (33 bytes), 48 bytes each ──
\ +0 the nonce (4 canonical words), +10 the amount, +18 the position (8;
\ all ones: not yet in the set), +20 the height it was made at, +24 the
\ state (0 unspent, 1 reserved, 2 spent), +25 the first leaf, +26 leaves
\ used, +27 recovered (found by a scan, not made here: its leaves the
\ second half's, as tabminer's), +28 the scan that last saw it (4 bytes),
\ +2C its kind (wnew's).

: okey variable ;  : orec variable ;  : wkl variable ;  : sgen variable ;
: ecom variable ;  : emem variable ;  : eamt variable ;  : epos variable ;  : eh variable ;  : ecb variable ;
: xk variable ;  : wxpk variable ;  : kseed variable ;  : scur variable ;  : scnt variable ;  : sfrom variable ;
: ltip variable ;  : ntip variable ;  : lh variable ;  : nodeok variable ;  : okn variable ;  : ppath variable ;
\ wgetk ( key klen buf n -- vlen )  in the writer's transaction.
: wgetk  wf2 !  wf1 !  wkl !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ wkl @ wf1 @ wf2 @ txget ;
: wsetk  wf2 !  wf1 !  wkl !  wgk !  wtx @ wgk @ wkl @ wf1 @ wf2 @ txput drop ;
\ wone  one output of the set (ecom, emem, eamt, epos, eh) checked: a
\ known one's position and scan noted; an unknown one with this wallet's
\ tag, its key derived and its commitment checked, recorded as found.
: wone
6F lit okey @ c!  ecom @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk 30 lit = if
	epos @ orec @ 18 lit + 8 lit bcopy  eh @ @ orec @ 20 lit + !  sgen @ orec @ 28 lit + !
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
else
	emem @ wkopen if
		kseed @ wkkey  kseed @ 4 lit xk @ xkgen  xk @ wxpk @ xkpub
		wxpk @ eamt @ ecb @ wkcom  ecb @ ecb @ 20 lit + wkcan
		ecb @ 20 lit + ecom @ 20 lit wssame if
			orec @ 30 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
			emem @ orec @ 10 lit bcopy  eamt @ orec @ 10 lit + 8 lit bcopy  epos @ orec @ 18 lit + 8 lit bcopy
			eh @ @ orec @ 20 lit + !  wtmp @ 1 lit wrand  wtmp @ c@ 7 lit and orec @ 25 lit + c!
			1 lit orec @ 27 lit + c!  sgen @ orec @ 28 lit + !
			okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
		then
	then
then ;
\ wpage ( -- n )  a page of the set from sfrom (8 bytes) checked: how many.
: wland
nlnd @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	lnd @ i 6 lit lshift + ecom @ 20 lit wssame if
		70 lit okey @ c!  lnd @ i 6 lit lshift + 20 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wgetk drop
		epos @ prec @ 94 lit + 8 lit bcopy  eh @ @ prec @ 9C lit + !
		okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wsetk
	then
loop then ;
\ wplist  the payments not yet landed (32 at most), their commitments and
\ ids at lnd (64 bytes each), for the scan to find.
: wplist
0 lit nlnd !
wfd @ 0 lit txbegin wtx !
70 lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 70 lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wgetk drop
	prec @ 98 lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit =  nlnd @ 20 lit u< and if
		prec @ 10 lit + lnd @ nlnd @ 6 lit lshift + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 1 lit + lnd @ nlnd @ 6 lit lshift + 20 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		nlnd @ 1 lit + nlnd !
	then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wtx @ txabort drop ;
: wpage
0 lit scnt !
ppath @ "/v1/outputs?from=" scpy  sfrom @ @ sfrom @ 4 lit + @ rot dstr "&count=1000" scpy 0 lit over c! drop
ppath @ hget dup scur !
if
	wbeg
	begin scur @ "'position':" jfind ?dup while
		jnum scur !  nlo @ epos @ !  nhi @ epos @ 4 lit + !
		scur @ "'commitment':'" jfind ecom @ 20 lit jhexb
		scur @ "'memo':'" jfind emem @ 14 lit jhexb
		scur @ "'amount':" jfind jnum drop  nlo @ eamt @ !  nhi @ eamt @ 4 lit + !
		scur @ "'height':" jfind jnum scur !  nlo @ eh @ !
		wone  wland  scnt @ 1 lit + scnt !
		\ the next page from the position after this one
		epos @ @ 1 lit + dup sfrom @ !  0= if epos @ 4 lit + @ 1 lit + else epos @ 4 lit + @ then sfrom @ 4 lit + !
	repeat
	wend drop
then
scnt @ ;
\ wspent  the outputs once in the set and not seen by this scan: spent.
: wspent
wbeg
6F lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 6F lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <>  orec @ 28 lit + @ sgen @ <> and  orec @ 24 lit + c@ 2 lit <> and if
		2 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
	then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wend drop ;
\ wscan ( -- ok )  the whole unspent set read through the node.
: wscan
"gen" wtmp @ 4 lit wget 4 lit = if wtmp @ @ else 0 lit then 1 lit + sgen !
0 lit sfrom @ !  0 lit sfrom @ 4 lit + !  1 lit nodeok !  wplist
begin wpage dup 0= if hres @ 0= if 0 lit nodeok ! then then 3E8 lit u< until
nodeok @ if
	wspent
	wbeg  sgen @ wtmp @ !  "gen" wtmp @ 4 lit wset  0 lit wtmp @ c!  "scan" wtmp @ 1 lit wset  wend drop
then
nodeok @ ;
\ wtick  the node asked for its tip; when it moved, the set scanned again
\ and the tip told (an event).
: wtick
have @ if
	"/v1/status" hget ?dup if
		dup "'height':" jfind jnum drop nlo @ lh !
		"'tip':'" jfind ntip @ 40 lit bcopy  0 lit ntip @ 40 lit + c!
		ntip @ ltip @ streq 0= if
			wscan if
				ltip @ ntip @ scpy 0 lit over c! drop
				"{'event':'tip','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec ",'hash':'" jo ltip @ jraw "'}" jo jend
			then
		then
	else 0 lit nodeok ! then
then ;
: wsum.  dup @ swap 4 lit + @ wamt ;                      \ ( acc -- )  written

: nowal  "no wallet yet: create or restore one" jerr ;

\ ── Payments (step 3): files, amounts, new outputs ──

: fbuf variable ;  : fn variable ;  : ffd variable ;
:M FMAX 8000 lit ;
\ fread ( path -- n | -1 )  a file of FMAX bytes at most into fbuf.
: fread
0 lit open dup ffd !  0< if FFFFFFFF lit else
	0 lit fn !
	begin ffd @ fbuf @ fn @ + FMAX fn @ - read  dup 0 lit > fn @ FMAX u< and while fn @ + fn ! repeat drop
	ffd @ close drop  fn @
then ;
\ fwrite ( path a n -- ok )  a file written whole (made, or emptied).
: fwa variable ;  : fwn variable ;
: fwrite
fwn !  fwa !  1 lit CREATE or TRUNC or open dup ffd !
0< if 0 lit else ffd @ fwa @ fwn @ write fwn @ =  ffd @ close drop then ;

\ Amounts, 8 bytes at an address.
: aa variable ;  : ab variable ;  : ad variable ;
\ a8add ( a b dst -- )  dst = a + b; a8sub ( a b dst -- ) dst = a - b.
: a8add
ad !  ab !  aa !
aa @ @ ab @ @ +  dup aa @ @ u< 1 lit and  aa @ 4 lit + @ +  ab @ 4 lit + @ +
ad @ 4 lit + !  ad @ ! ;
: a8sub
ad !  ab !  aa !
aa @ @ ab @ @ -  aa @ @ ab @ @ u< 1 lit and  aa @ 4 lit + @ ab @ 4 lit + @ - swap -
ad @ 4 lit + !  ad @ ! ;
\ a8lt ( a b -- flag )  a below b.
: a8lt
ab !  aa !
aa @ 4 lit + @ ab @ 4 lit + @ = if aa @ @ ab @ @ u< else aa @ 4 lit + @ ab @ 4 lit + @ u< then ;
\ a8set ( lo hi dst -- )
: a8set  ad !  ad @ 4 lit + !  ad @ ! ;

\ jcoins ( s dst -- ok )  coins as text (up to ten decimals) into base
\ units at dst.
: jcs variable ;  : jcd variable ;  : jcn variable ;  : jcf variable ;  : jck variable ;
: jcs+  jcs @ 1 lit + jcs ! ;
: jdig?  jcs @ c@ 30 lit - A lit u< ;
: jcoins
jcd !  jcs !  0 lit nlo !  0 lit nhi !  0 lit jcn !  0 lit jcf !  -1 lit jck !
begin jdig? while jcs @ c@ 30 lit - d10+ jcs+ jcn @ 1 lit + jcn ! repeat
jcs @ c@ 2E lit = if
	jcs+
	begin jdig? while jcs @ c@ 30 lit - d10+ jcs+ jcn @ 1 lit + jcn !  jcf @ 1 lit + jcf ! repeat
then
jcf @ A lit u> if 0 lit jck ! then
jcs @ c@ if 0 lit jck ! then
jcn @ 0= if 0 lit jck ! then
jck @ if A lit jcf @ - ?dup if 0 lit do 0 lit d10+ loop then then
nlo @ nhi @ jcd @ a8set  jck @ ;

\ wrfp ( a -- )  a random field element (below p) at a.
: wrfp
begin wtmp @ 4 lit wrand  wtmp @ @ 7FFFFFFF lit and  dup 78000001 lit u< 0= while drop repeat
swap ! ;
\ wnew ( amt kind -- )  a new output of this wallet's, in the writer's
\ transaction: a random nonce, its key, its memo; onew the output (60
\ bytes), ecom its commitment; recorded as not yet in the set (kind: 0
\ found, 1 received by an answer, 2 change).
: wna variable ;  : wnk variable ;  : nb variable ;  : wmb variable ;  : onew variable ;
: wnew
wnk !  wna !
4 lit 0 lit do nb @ i 2 lit lshift + wrfp loop
nb @ wknon  kseed @ wkkey  kseed @ 4 lit xk @ xkgen  xk @ wxpk @ xkpub  wmb @ wkmemo
wxpk @ wna @ wmb @ onew @ wsmkout
wxpk @ wna @ ecb @ wkcom  ecb @ ecom @ wkcan
orec @ 30 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
nb @ orec @ 10 lit bcopy  wna @ orec @ 10 lit + 8 lit bcopy
FFFFFFFF lit orec @ 18 lit + !  FFFFFFFF lit orec @ 1C lit + !  wnk @ orec @ 2C lit + c!
6F lit okey @ c!  ecom @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk ;

\ ── Slates as text (as tabminer's, docs/GUI_WALLET.md): base64 of the
\ slate's bytes between "-----BEGIN TAB SLATE-----" and its END line, 64
\ characters a line ──

: bmb variable ;  : bme variable ;
\ bslate, boffer: the markers b64out writes and b64in looks for, a
\ slate's or a name offer's (-----BEGIN TAB NAME OFFER-----, as tabminer's).
: bslate  "-----BEGIN TAB SLATE-----" bmb !  "-----END TAB SLATE-----" bme ! ;
: boffer  "-----BEGIN TAB NAME OFFER-----" bmb !  "-----END TAB NAME OFFER-----" bme ! ;
: bjs variable ;  : bbp variable ;  : bcol variable ;  : bsn variable ;  : bsv variable ;  : bsrc variable ;
: bacc variable ;  : bscnt variable ;  : bdst variable ;  : bdn variable ;  : bpad variable ;
\ bput ( c -- )  a byte of the text: into the answer (bjs), else at bbp.
: bput  bjs @ if jc else bbp @ c!  bbp @ 1 lit + bbp ! then ;
\ bnl  a line's end: escaped in the answer.
: bnl  bjs @ if 5C lit jc 6E lit jc else A lit bput then ;
: bmark  ?dup if 0 lit do dup i + c@ bput loop then drop ;   \ ( s n -- )
: b64c  "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/" + c@ ;   \ ( v -- c )
: bchar  bput  bcol @ 1 lit + dup bcol !  40 lit = if bnl 0 lit bcol ! then ;
\ b64out ( a n -- )  a slate's bytes as text: each group of three bytes
\ four characters, a short last group padded with '='.
: bln variable ;  : bsbad variable ;
: b64out
bsn !  bsrc !  0 lit bcol !
bmb @ dup strlen bmark bnl
bsn @ 2 lit + 3 lit / ?dup if 0 lit do
	bsn @ i 3 lit * - 3 lit umin bln !
	bsrc @ i 3 lit * + bsv !
	bsv @ c@ 10 lit lshift
	bln @ 1 lit u> if bsv @ 1 lit + c@ 8 lit lshift or then
	bln @ 2 lit u> if bsv @ 2 lit + c@ or then
	bacc !
	4 lit 0 lit do
		i bln @ u> if 3D lit bchar else bacc @ 12 lit i 6 lit * - rshift 3F lit and b64c bchar then
	loop
loop then
bcol @ if bnl then
bme @ dup strlen bmark bnl ;
\ b64v ( c -- v | -1 )  a base64 character's value ('=' 0).
: b64v
dup 41 lit - 1A lit u< if 41 lit - else dup 61 lit - 1A lit u< if 61 lit - 1A lit + else
dup 30 lit - A lit u< if 30 lit - 34 lit + else dup 2B lit = if drop 3E lit else
dup 2F lit = if drop 3F lit else 3D lit = if 0 lit else FFFFFFFF lit then then then then then then ;
\ b64in ( text dst -- n | -1 )  the slate's bytes from text holding one
\ between its markers, whatever surrounds it (whitespace skipped).
: b64in
bdst !  bmb @ jfind dup if
	0 lit bdn !  0 lit bacc !  0 lit bscnt !  0 lit bpad !  0 lit bsbad !
	begin dup c@ dup 0= 0= swap 2D lit <> and while
		dup c@ 20 lit u> if
			dup c@ 3D lit = if bpad @ 1 lit + bpad ! then
			dup c@ b64v dup 0< if
				\ not base64: the rest passed over
				2drop 1 lit bsbad !  ""
			else
				bacc @ 6 lit lshift or bacc !  bscnt @ 1 lit + bscnt !
				bscnt @ 4 lit = if
					bacc @ 10 lit rshift bdst @ bdn @ + c!  bacc @ 8 lit rshift bdst @ bdn @ + 1 lit + c!  bacc @ bdst @ bdn @ + 2 lit + c!
					bdn @ 3 lit + bpad @ - bdn !  0 lit bscnt !  0 lit bacc !  0 lit bpad !
				then
				1 lit +
			then
		else 1 lit + then
	repeat
	c@ 2D lit =  bsbad @ 0= and  bscnt @ 0= and if bdn @ else FFFFFFFF lit then
else drop FFFFFFFF lit then ;

\ wrget ( key klen buf n -- vlen )  one record, read in a snapshot.
: wrget  wf2 !  wf1 !  wkl !  wgk !  wfd @ 0 lit txbegin  dup wgk @ wkl @ wf1 @ wf2 @ txget  swap txabort drop ;
\ rpkey ( k -- )  okey (34 bytes) = "q", the id at okey+1 kept, part k.
: rpkey  okey @ 21 lit + c!  71 lit okey @ c! ;
: rplen  RPART * 148D lit swap - RPART umin ;            \ ( k -- n )
\ wrcpt+ ( -- )  the receipt at prec+DC written in its parts, in the
\ writer's transaction (okey+1 the id); wrcpt ( -- ) read back to prec+DC.
: wrcpt+  6 lit 0 lit do i rpkey  okey @ 22 lit prec @ DC lit + i RPART * + i rplen wsetk loop  70 lit okey @ c! ;
: wrcpt  6 lit 0 lit do i rpkey  okey @ 22 lit prec @ DC lit + i RPART * + i rplen wrget drop loop  70 lit okey @ c! ;
\ jhex ( a n -- )  n bytes written in hex.
: jhd  F lit and dup A lit u< if 30 lit + else 57 lit + then jc ;
: jhex  ?dup if 0 lit do dup i + c@ dup 4 lit rshift jhd jhd loop then drop ;
: a8.  dup @ swap 4 lit + @ wamt ;                     \ ( a -- )  in coins, written
: fpath variable ;  : fout variable ;  : fpn variable ;

\ A slate is text wherever a person handles it (base64 between its
\ markers, as tabminer's: it has no other form outside the wallet).  A
\ slate in: slin ( line -- n | -1 ) its bytes at sbin, pasted ("text",
\ tmode 1) or from a file ("slate", tmode 0); -1 none given, or none in
\ it.  A slate out: sout ( a n path -- ok ) as text to a file; stext ( a
\ n -- ) as text, written in the answer.
: sbin variable ;  : ttxt variable ;  : tout variable ;  : tmode variable ;
: slin
bslate
dup "'text':'" ttxt @ 2400 lit jstr if
	drop 1 lit tmode !  ttxt @ sbin @ b64in
else
	0 lit tmode !
	"'slate':'" fpath @ 100 lit jstr 0= if FFFFFFFF lit else
		fpath @ fread dup 0< 0= if
			0 lit swap fbuf @ + c!  fbuf @ sbin @ b64in
		then
	then
then ;
: stext  bslate  1 lit bjs !  b64out  0 lit bjs ! ;
: sop variable ;  : soa variable ;  : son variable ;
: sout
sop !  son !  soa !  bslate
0 lit bjs !  tout @ bbp !  soa @ son @ b64out  sop @ tout @ bbp @ tout @ - fwrite ;
\ oanswer ( line -- )  a payer's slate (stage 1) answered: this wallet's
\ output added and recorded, its receipt signed, the answer written to
\ the file's name and ".received" (as tabminer's receive).
: oanswer
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
slin fpn !  fpn @ 0< if "no slate given, or not one" jerr else
sbin @ fpn @ wsparse 0= if "not a slate" jerr else
wsstg @ 1 lit <> if "not a slate to answer" jerr else
wsnout @ wschg @ <> if "the slate is answered already" jerr else
	waddr!
	wbeg  wsa @ 49 lit + 1 lit wnew  wend
	if
		onew @ wsk @ wpk @ wsans fpn !
		tmode @ if
			jok ",'text':'" jo wsbuf @ fpn @ stext "','amount':'" jo wsa @ 49 lit + a8. "'}" jo jend
		else
			fout @ fpath @ scpy ".received" scpy 0 lit over c! drop
			wsbuf @ fpn @ fout @ sout if
				jok ",'slate':'" jo fout @ jraw "','amount':'" jo wsa @ 49 lit + a8. "'}" jo jend
			else "the answer cannot be written" jerr then
		then
	else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
then then then then then ;

\ The fees: /v1/fees's rates (a byte) for a block, an hour, a day, and
\ economy.
: frk variable ;
\ frate ( body speed -- rate )  a speed's rate (10, the floor, if unknown).
: frate
frk @ "'" scpy swap scpy "':{'rate':" scpy 0 lit over c! drop
frk @ jfind ?dup if jnum drop nlo @ else A lit then ;
: ofees
"/v1/fees" hget ?dup 0= if "the node is not reached" jerr else
	jok ",'speeds':[{'speed':'block','rate':" jo dup "block" frate 0 lit wdec
	",'wait':600},{'speed':'hour','rate':" jo dup "hour" frate 0 lit wdec
	",'wait':3600},{'speed':'day','rate':" jo dup "day" frate 0 lit wdec
	",'wait':86400},{'speed':'economy','rate':" jo "economy" frate 0 lit wdec ",'wait':604800}]}" jo jend
then ;

\ The coins to spend: sel, entries of 40 bytes (the commitment, the
\ amount), largest first; nsel of them.
: sel variable ;  : nsel variable ;  : se variable ;  : sk variable ;
: selent  6 lit lshift sel @ + ;                         \ ( i -- a )
\ wsels  the confirmed unspent outputs gathered, sorted: 28 at most, as a
\ payment's pending record (its inputs' commitments) must fit the store's
\ 1 KiB values.
: wsels
0 lit nsel !
wfd @ 0 lit txbegin wtx !
6F lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 6F lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	orec @ 24 lit + c@ 0=  orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <> and  nsel @ 1C lit u< and if
		okey @ 1 lit + nsel @ selent 20 lit bcopy  orec @ 10 lit + nsel @ selent 20 lit + 8 lit bcopy
		nsel @ 1 lit + nsel !
	then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wtx @ txabort drop
\ largest first: each place takes the largest of those after it
nsel @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i se !
	nsel @ i do  se @ selent 20 lit + i selent 20 lit + a8lt if i se ! then  loop
	se @ i <> if
		i selent wtmp @ 40 lit bcopy  se @ selent i selent 40 lit bcopy  wtmp @ se @ selent 40 lit bcopy
	then
loop then ;

\ The payment's numbers, 8 bytes each: the amount, the fee, what is
\ needed, what the coins picked hold, the change; the rate, the inputs.
: samt variable ;  : sfee variable ;  : sneed variable ;  : stot variable ;  : schg variable ;
: srate variable ;  : snin variable ;  : spick variable ;  : sdone variable ;  : sdust variable ;
: pend variable ;  : sid variable ;  : ssec variable ;  : ssnd variable ;  : pkb variable ;
\ spick! ( -- )  coins taken largest first until they hold sneed: spick of
\ them, stot their sum.
: spick!
0 lit spick !  0 lit stot @ !  0 lit stot @ 4 lit + !
begin spick @ nsel @ u<  stot @ sneed @ a8lt and while
	stot @ spick @ selent 20 lit + stot @ a8add  spick @ 1 lit + spick !
repeat ;
\ wfee  sfee = the rate times a payment's size with snin inputs (16 +
\ 2,377 each + two outputs of 60), sneed = samt + sfee.
: wfee  snin @ 949 lit * 88 lit +  srate @ *  0 lit sfee @ a8set  samt @ sfee @ sneed @ a8add ;
\ wpkof ( commitment dst -- )  an output's public key (49 bytes): its key
\ derived from its record's nonce.
: wpkof
swap 6F lit okey @ c!  okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wrget drop
orec @ wknon  kseed @ wkkey  kseed @ 4 lit xk @ xkgen  xk @ swap xkpub ;
\ osend ( line -- )  a payment begun by file: coins picked, change made,
\ the coins reserved and the payment recorded in one transaction, the
\ stage-1 slate written for the recipient.  The sender is unnamed (the
\ hash of a secret kept, docs/PRIVACY.md).
\ (wmon set: the slate made for osonl to send online, wmok set, nothing
\ answered.)
: wmon variable ;  : wmok variable ;
: osend
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup "'amount':'" wtmp @ 40 lit jstr  wtmp @ samt @ jcoins and 0= if drop "not an amount" jerr else
samt @ sdust @ a8lt if drop "the amount is below the dust limit" jerr else
dup "'text':true" jfind 0= 0= tmode !  0 lit fpath @ c!  dup "'slate':'" fpath @ 100 lit jstr drop
tmode @ fpath @ c@ or wmon @ or 0= if drop "no slate file, nor text asked for" jerr else
"'speed':'" wtmp @ 20 lit jstr drop
"/v1/fees" hget ?dup if wtmp @ frate else A lit then srate !
wsels
1 lit snin !  0 lit sdone !
begin sdone @ 0= while
	wfee spick!
	stot @ sneed @ a8lt if 2 lit sdone ! else
	spick @ snin @ u> if spick @ snin ! else 1 lit sdone ! then then
repeat
sdone @ 2 lit = if "not enough confirmed coins" jerr else
	\ the change, or below the dust limit, the fee's
	stot @ sneed @ schg @ a8sub
	schg @ sdust @ a8lt if sfee @ schg @ sfee @ a8add  0 lit 0 lit schg @ a8set then
	sid @ 20 lit wrand  ssec @ 20 lit wrand  ssec @ wsd @ wstag  wsd @ ssnd @ wkcan
	\ the record: inputs, change, amount, fee, sender, secret, change's
	\ commitment, the inputs' commitments
	pend @ 78 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
	spick @ pend @ !  samt @ pend @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy  sfee @ pend @ 10 lit + 8 lit bcopy
	ssnd @ pend @ 18 lit + 20 lit bcopy  ssec @ pend @ 38 lit + 20 lit bcopy
	spick @ 0 lit do i selent pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + 20 lit bcopy loop
	wbeg
	schg @ @ schg @ 4 lit + @ or if
		schg @ 2 lit wnew  1 lit pend @ 4 lit + !  ecom @ pend @ 58 lit + 20 lit bcopy
	then
	spick @ 0 lit do
		6F lit okey @ c!  i selent okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop  1 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
	loop
	73 lit okey @ c!  sid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit pend @ 78 lit spick @ 5 lit lshift + wsetk
	wend if
		\ the slate: its inputs' keys derived, its change
		sid @ ssnd @ samt @ sfee @ wsbeg
		spick @ 0 lit do  i selent pkb @ wpkof  pkb @ i selent 20 lit + wsaddin  loop
		pend @ 4 lit + @ if onew @ wsaddout then
		pend @ 4 lit + @ wsfix fpn !
		wmon @ if -1 lit wmok ! else
		tmode @ if
			jok ",'text':'" jo wsbuf @ fpn @ stext "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
		else wsbuf @ fpn @ fpath @ sout if
			jok ",'slate':'" jo fpath @ jraw "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
		else "the slate cannot be written" jerr then then then
	else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
then
then then then then ;

\ The sent records, "x" || a transaction's id (33 bytes): what cancel and
\ bump re-sign.  +0 its inputs (n), +4 1 if it has change, +8 its fee
\ (8), +10 its size, +18 the change's commitment, +38 the inputs'
\ commitments, 32 bytes each (28 at most: under the store's 1 KiB).
\ wxput ( n -- )  the record of the transaction ecb written, in the
\ writer's transaction: n inputs (their commitments at xsrc, xst apart),
\ +4 to +37 as the caller set them.
: xrec variable ;  : xsrc variable ;  : xst variable ;  : xid variable ;  : xout variable ;  : xsz variable ;
: wxput
dup xrec @ !  ?dup if 0 lit do xsrc @ xst @ i * + xrec @ 38 lit + i 5 lit lshift + 20 lit bcopy loop then
78 lit okey @ c!  ecb @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit xrec @ 38 lit xrec @ @ 5 lit lshift + wsetk ;
: xzero  xrec @ 38 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop ;

\ ofinb ( -- )  the slate at sbin (fpn bytes) finalized, as ofinal.
\ ofinal ( line -- )  the recipient's answer finalized: tabminer's checks
\ against the payment's record (wsfin); each input's next leaf recorded as
\ used, committed, before any signature is made; the transaction signed
\ and sent to the node; accepted, the inputs spent, the payment recorded.
: fkeys variable ;  : fka variable ;  : flv variable ;  : fps variable ;  : pins variable ;  : fchg variable ;
: fcode variable ;  : fnin variable ;  : ftx variable ;  : fbad variable ;
\ wfmsg ( code -- )  wsfin's refusal answered.
: wfmsg
dup 1 lit = if drop "not an answered slate" else dup 2 lit = if drop "its inputs changed" else
dup 3 lit = if drop "no output for the recipient" else dup 4 lit = if drop "its amount or fee changed" else
dup 5 lit = if drop "its amounts do not balance" else dup 6 lit = if drop "its change changed" else
dup 7 lit = if drop "an output is zero or below the dust limit" else dup 8 lit = if drop "it is too large" else
9 lit = if "not one output for the recipient" else "the receipt does not hold" then
then then then then then then then then jerr ;
: ofinb
sbin @ fpn @ wsparse 0= if "not a slate" jerr else
73 lit okey @ c!  wsa @ 8 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit pend @ 878 lit wrget 0< if "not a payment this wallet began" jerr else
	pend @ @ fnin !  0 lit fbad !
	\ the inputs: keys, public keys and amounts, leaves, positions
	fnin @ 0 lit do
		6F lit okey @ c!  pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wrget drop
		orec @ wknon  kseed @ wkkey  fkeys @ i 440 lit * + dup fka @ i 2 lit lshift + !
		kseed @ 4 lit rot xkgen
		fka @ i 2 lit lshift + @ pins @ i 39 lit * + xkpub  orec @ 10 lit + pins @ i 39 lit * + 31 lit + 8 lit bcopy
		orec @ 18 lit + fps @ i 3 lit lshift + 8 lit bcopy
		orec @ 26 lit + c@ 8 lit u< 0= if 1 lit fbad ! then
		orec @ 25 lit + c@ orec @ 26 lit + c@ + 7 lit and  orec @ 27 lit + c@ if 8 lit + then  flv @ i 2 lit lshift + !
	loop
	\ the change output as made
	0 lit fchg !
	pend @ 4 lit + @ if
		pend @ 58 lit + pkb @ wpkof
		orec @ wknon  wmb @ wkmemo  pkb @ orec @ 10 lit + wmb @ onew @ wsmkout  onew @ fchg !
	then
	fbad @ if "an input has signed all it may" jerr else
	pins @ fnin @ pend @ 8 lit + pend @ 10 lit + fchg @ pend @ 18 lit + wsfin dup fcode !
	if fcode @ wfmsg else
		\ the leaves used, recorded before any signature
		wbeg
		fnin @ 0 lit do
			6F lit okey @ c!  pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
			okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
			orec @ 26 lit + c@ 1 lit + orec @ 26 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
		loop
		wend 0= if "the wallet could not be written" jerr else
			fka @ flv @ fps @ wstx ftx !
			"POST" "/v1/tx" wstxb @ ftx @ hask
			hcode @ C8 lit = if
				drop
				\ spent, the payment recorded (by its id: the body hash)
				wsd @ wsbody  wsd @ ecb @ wkcan
				wbeg
				fnin @ 0 lit do
					6F lit okey @ c!  pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
					okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop  2 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
				loop
				73 lit okey @ c!  wsa @ 8 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop
				prec @ PREC 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
				pend @ 8 lit + prec @ 8 lit bcopy  pend @ 10 lit + prec @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy
				wsouts @ wschg @ 3C lit * + wsd @ wsocom  wsd @ prec @ 10 lit + wkcan
				wsa @ 8 lit + prec @ 30 lit + 20 lit bcopy  pend @ 18 lit + prec @ 50 lit + 20 lit bcopy
				1 lit prec @ 70 lit + !  pend @ 38 lit + prec @ 74 lit + 20 lit bcopy
				FFFFFFFF lit prec @ 94 lit + !  FFFFFFFF lit prec @ 98 lit + !
				wsouts @ wschg @ 3C lit * + prec @ A0 lit + 3C lit bcopy  wsrc @ prec @ DC lit + 148D lit bcopy
				70 lit okey @ c!  ecb @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wsetk  wrcpt+
				xzero  pend @ 4 lit + @ xrec @ 4 lit + !  pend @ 10 lit + xrec @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy  ftx @ xrec @ 10 lit + !
				pend @ 58 lit + xrec @ 18 lit + 20 lit bcopy  pend @ 78 lit + xsrc !  20 lit xst !  fnin @ wxput  70 lit okey @ c!
				wend drop
				jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo pend @ 10 lit + a8. "'}" jo jend
			else
				?dup if "'reason':'" wtmp @ 100 lit jstr drop wtmp @ jsafe "the node refused it: " wtmp @ 100 lit + swap scpy wtmp @ scpy 0 lit over c! drop wtmp @ 100 lit + jerr
				else "the node is not reached" jerr then
			then
		then
	then then
then then ;
: ofinal
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
slin fpn !  fpn @ 0< if "no slate given, or not one" jerr else ofinb then
then ;

\ ── Proofs and burns (phase 2, docs/PROOFS.md) ──

\ The coins a transaction spends (wib, wist apart, win of them): their
\ keys (fka), leaves (flv), positions (fps).  winp ( -- bad ) them made
\ (bad: one has signed all it may); wleaf+ ( -- ok ) their next leaves
\ recorded as used, committed before any signature; wspend+ marks them
\ spent in the writer's transaction.
: wib variable ;  : wist variable ;  : win variable ;  : wibad variable ;
: wicom  wist @ * wib @ + ;                              \ ( i -- a )
: wirec  6F lit okey @ c!  wicom okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy ;   \ ( i -- )  okey
: winp
0 lit wibad !
win @ 0 lit do
	i wirec  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wrget drop
	orec @ wknon  kseed @ wkkey  fkeys @ i 440 lit * + dup fka @ i 2 lit lshift + !
	kseed @ 4 lit rot xkgen
	orec @ 18 lit + fps @ i 3 lit lshift + 8 lit bcopy
	orec @ 26 lit + c@ 8 lit u< 0= if 1 lit wibad ! then
	orec @ 25 lit + c@ orec @ 26 lit + c@ + 7 lit and  orec @ 27 lit + c@ if 8 lit + then  flv @ i 2 lit lshift + !
loop
wibad @ ;
: wleaf+
wbeg
win @ 0 lit do
	i wirec  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	orec @ 26 lit + c@ 1 lit + orec @ 26 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
loop
wend ;
: wspend+  win @ 0 lit do i wirec  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop  2 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk loop ;

\ jtxt ( a n -- )  text written as a JSON string's characters.
: jtxt  ?dup if 0 lit do dup i + c@
	dup A lit = if drop 5C lit jc 6E lit jc else dup 22 lit = over 5C lit = or if 5C lit jc jc else jc then then
loop then drop ;

\ wpget ( -- ok )  ppth (1,280 bytes) = the path of the payment in prec's
\ output (+94 its position, +9C its height) to that block's state root,
\ from the node (/v1/proof/output/<position>?at=<height>).
: ppth variable ;  : pcur variable ;
: wpget
ppath @ "/v1/proof/output/" scpy  prec @ 94 lit + @ prec @ 98 lit + @ rot dstr "?at=" scpy
prec @ 9C lit + @ 0 lit rot dstr drop
ppath @ hget ?dup if
	dup "'commitment':'" jfind if
		"'siblings':[" jfind ?dup if
			pcur !
			28 lit 0 lit do
				pcur @ begin dup c@ 22 lit <> over c@ and while 1 lit + repeat 1 lit +
				dup ppth @ i 5 lit lshift + 20 lit jhexb  41 lit + pcur !
			loop
			-1 lit
		else 0 lit then
	else drop 0 lit then
else 0 lit then ;

\ oproof ( line -- )  a payment's or burn's proof (its id in "tx"), once
\ its output has landed: as text, to give whoever asks.
: pftxt variable ;  : pbin variable ;
: oproof
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
"'tx':'" wtmp @ 50 lit jstr 0= if "no transaction id" jerr else
wtmp @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit jhexb  70 lit okey @ c!
okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wrget 0< if "no payment or burn with that id" jerr else
prec @ 98 lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit = if "not in a block yet: a proof is made once it is" jerr else
wpget 0= if "the node gives no path for it (is it synced?)" jerr else
	prec @ 70 lit + @ 2 lit = if 2 lit else 1 lit then
	prec @ 9C lit + @  prec @ 94 lit +  prec @ A0 lit +  prec @ C0 lit +  prec @ C8 lit + wphdr
	ppth @ wppath
	prec @ 70 lit + @ 2 lit = if
		0 lit rpkey  okey @ 22 lit prec @ DC lit + 100 lit wrget drop  70 lit okey @ c!
		prec @ 50 lit +  prec @ 74 lit +  prec @ DD lit +  prec @ DC lit + c@ wpburn
	else
		wrcpt  1 lit  prec @ 74 lit +  prec @ 30 lit +  prec @ DC lit +  prec @ DC lit + 7A0 lit + wppay
	then
	wpb @ swap pftxt @ wptext
	jok ",'proof':'" jo pftxt @ swap jtxt "'}" jo jend
then then then then then ;

\ overify ( line -- )  a proof (pasted, "text") checked against the node's
\ header at its height: valid or not, and why; what it shows (a burn's
\ purpose and beneficiary, a payment's receiver).
: vroot variable ;  : waddr2 variable ;
: overify
"'text':'" pftxt @ 3000 lit jstr 0= if "no proof given" jerr else
pftxt @ pbin @ wpfrom dup 0< if drop "no proof in it" jerr else
pbin @ swap wpparse 0= if "not a proof" jerr else
	ppath @ "/v1/header/" scpy  wpa @ 1 lit + le@ 0 lit rot dstr drop
	ppath @ hget ?dup if
		"'state_root':'" jfind ?dup if vroot @ 20 lit jhexb
			vroot @ wpchk
			jok ",'valid':" jo dup 0= if "true" else "false" then jo
			",'reason':'" jo dup 0= if drop "it holds" else dup 1 lit = if drop "the output is not in that block" else
				2 lit = if "the receipt does not hold" else "not that burn" then then then jo
			"','kind':'" jo wpfmt @ 2 lit = if "burn" else "payment" then jo
			"','amount':'" jo wpa @ 2D lit + a8.  "','height':" jo wpa @ 1 lit + le@ 0 lit wdec
			wpfmt @ 2 lit = if
				\ the purpose (its bytes after the beneficiary and nonce), made safe
				wpa @ WPCL + 41 lit +  pftxt @  wpa @ WPCL + 40 lit + c@ bcopy  0 lit pftxt @ wpa @ WPCL + 40 lit + c@ + c!
				pftxt @ jsafe  ",'purpose':'" jo pftxt @ jo "'" jo
				",'for':'" jo  wpa @ WPCL + wsd @ dle
			else
				",'to':'" jo  wpa @ WPCL + 41 lit + wsd @ wkid
			then
			wsd @ waddr2 @ wkaddr  waddr2 @ jraw "'}" jo jend
		else "the node has no header at that height" jerr then
	else "the node is not reached" jerr then
then then then ;
\ wcarry ( -- code )  a transaction of the wallet's own: coins chosen
\ (as a payment's) for samt (an amount the extra output takes, or 0) and
\ the fee at srate; a change output (below the dust limit, the fee's);
\ the extra output wcx (60 bytes, or 0: a burn's); the operation at wco
\ (wcon bytes, or none: a name's); signed (the leaves recorded first),
\ posted to the node.  0: done (its id canonical at ecb, the fee sfee, the
\ inputs spent); 2 not enough coins, 3 an input has signed all it may, 4
\ the wallet not written, 5 refused by the node (why at wcwhy), 6 the node
\ not reached.
: wcx variable ;  : wco variable ;  : wcon variable ;  : wcwhy variable ;  : bchg variable ;
: wcarry
wsels
1 lit snin !  0 lit sdone !
begin sdone @ 0= while
	wfee  wcon @ srate @ * 0 lit wtmp @ a8set  sneed @ wtmp @ sneed @ a8add  sfee @ wtmp @ sfee @ a8add
	spick!
	stot @ sneed @ a8lt if 2 lit sdone ! else
	spick @ snin @ u> if spick @ snin ! else 1 lit sdone ! then then
repeat
sdone @ 2 lit = if 2 lit else
	stot @ sneed @ schg @ a8sub
	schg @ sdust @ a8lt if sfee @ schg @ sfee @ a8add  0 lit 0 lit schg @ a8set then
	0 lit bchg !  xzero
	schg @ @ schg @ 4 lit + @ or if wbeg  schg @ 2 lit wnew  wend drop  1 lit bchg !  ecom @ xrec @ 18 lit + 20 lit bcopy then
	sel @ wib !  40 lit wist !  spick @ win !
	wcbeg
	win @ 0 lit do  i wicom pkb @ wpkof  pkb @ i wicom 20 lit + wcin+  loop
	bchg @ if onew @ wcout+ then  wcx @ ?dup if wcout+ then  wcon @ if wco @ wcon @ wcop+ then
	winp if 3 lit else
	wleaf+ 0= if 4 lit else
		fka @ flv @ fps @ wctx ftx !
		"POST" "/v1/tx" wctb @ ftx @ hask
		hcode @ C8 lit = if
			drop  wsd @ wcbody  wsd @ ecb @ wkcan
			wbeg wspend+
			\ a payment's or burn's (no operation): its sent record, for cancel and bump
			wcon @ 0= if
				bchg @ xrec @ 4 lit + !  sfee @ xrec @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy  ftx @ xrec @ 10 lit + !
				sel @ xsrc !  40 lit xst !  win @ wxput
			then
			wend drop  0 lit
		else
			?dup if "'reason':'" wcwhy @ 100 lit jstr drop wcwhy @ jsafe 5 lit else 6 lit then
		then
	then then
then ;
\ wcerr ( code -- )  wcarry's failure answered.
: wcerr
dup 2 lit = if drop "not enough confirmed coins" jerr else dup 3 lit = if drop "an input has signed all it may" jerr else
dup 4 lit = if drop "the wallet could not be written" jerr else
5 lit = if wtmp @ "the node refused it: " scpy wcwhy @ scpy 0 lit over c! drop wtmp @ jerr else "the node is not reached" jerr then
then then then ;
: wspeed  "'speed':'" wtmp @ 20 lit jstr drop  "/v1/fees" hget ?dup if wtmp @ frate else A lit then srate ! ;   \ ( line -- )

\ oburn ( line -- )  coins burned (docs/PROOFS.md): "amount", "purpose"
\ (255 bytes at most), "for" (a tab1 address: whom the burn credits; this
\ wallet's own if none), "speed".  As tabminer's burn: coins chosen as a
\ payment's, a change output, the burned output (key hash zero, its memo
\ the hash of the beneficiary, a random nonce and the purpose); signed and
\ sent to the node, recorded as a payment (kind 2) for its proof.
: bben variable ;  : bnon variable ;  : bpur variable ;  : bpl variable ;  : bburn variable ;
: oburn
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup "'amount':'" wtmp @ 40 lit jstr  wtmp @ samt @ jcoins and 0= if drop "not an amount" jerr else
samt @ sdust @ a8lt if drop "the amount is below the dust limit" jerr else
dup "'purpose':'" bpur @ 100 lit jstr 0= if drop "a purpose is needed (255 bytes at most)" jerr else
dup "'for':'" wtmp @ 80 lit jstr wtmp @ c@ 0= 0= and if
	wtmp @ wsd @ wkdec
else waddr! wpk @ wsd @ wkid -1 lit then
0= if drop "not a tab1 address" jerr else
	wsd @ bben @ wkcan  bpur @ strlen bpl !
	wspeed
	\ the burned output: key hash zero, the amount, its memo
	bnon @ 20 lit wrand  bben @ bnon @ bpur @ bpl @ bburn @ 28 lit + wpbmemo
	bburn @ 20 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop  samt @ bburn @ 20 lit + 8 lit bcopy
	bburn @ wcx !  0 lit wcon !
	wcarry ?dup if wcerr else
		wbeg
		prec @ PREC 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
		samt @ prec @ 8 lit bcopy  sfee @ prec @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy
		bburn @ wsd @ wsocom  wsd @ prec @ 10 lit + wkcan
		bben @ prec @ 50 lit + 20 lit bcopy  2 lit prec @ 70 lit + !  bnon @ prec @ 74 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		FFFFFFFF lit prec @ 94 lit + !  FFFFFFFF lit prec @ 98 lit + !  bburn @ prec @ A0 lit + 3C lit bcopy
		70 lit okey @ c!  ecb @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wsetk
		bpl @ prec @ DC lit + c!  bpur @ prec @ DD lit + bpl @ bcopy
		0 lit rpkey  okey @ 22 lit prec @ DC lit + bpl @ 1 lit + wsetk  70 lit okey @ c!
		wend drop
		jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
	then
then then then then then ;

\ ── Names (phase 2, docs/NAMES.md), as tabminer's wallet: records "n" ||
\ the name, 88h bytes: +0 the nonce (its owner key, salt and memo come
\ from it), +10 the value (32, canonical), +30 the stage (0 committed, 1
\ revealed, 2 owned), +31 the first leaf, +32 leaves used, +33 recovered,
\ +34 an update pending, +38 the commit (32, canonical), +58 the pending
\ update's nonce, +68 its value. ──
:M NRECN 88 lit ;
: nrecb variable ;  : nname variable ;  : nlen variable ;  : nown variable ;  : nownc variable ;  : nsalt variable ;
: nsaltc variable ;  : nnh variable ;  : ncom variable ;  : ncomc variable ;  : nmem variable ;  : nopb variable ;
: nrb variable ;  : nrl variable ;  : nval variable ;  : ncpos variable ;  : ncht variable ;  : nfnd variable ;  : nmlv variable ;
: nmkey  6E lit okey @ c!  nname @ okey @ 1 lit + nlen @ bcopy ;           \ okey: "n" || the name
: nmget  nmkey  okey @ nlen @ 1 lit + nrecb @ NRECN wrget NRECN = ;        \ ( -- flag )
: nmput  nmkey  okey @ nlen @ 1 lit + nrecb @ NRECN wsetk ;                \ in the writer's transaction
\ nderive ( nonce -- )  from a name's nonce (and nname): the owner (nown,
\ nownc), the salt (nsalt, nsaltc), the name's hash, the commit (ncom,
\ ncomc), the memo (nmem, 32 canonical bytes).
: nderive
wknon  nown @ wnown  nown @ nownc @ wkcan  nsalt @ wnsalt  nsalt @ nsaltc @ wkcan
nname @ nlen @ nnh @ wnhash  nnh @ nsalt @ nown @ ncom @ wncom  ncom @ ncomc @ wkcan  nmem @ wnmemo ;
\ nname? ( line -- ok )  the request's name (nname, nlen), valid.
: nname?  "'name':'" nname @ 40 lit jstr  nname @ strlen dup nlen !  nname @ swap wnok and ;
\ nvalue ( line -- ok )  the request's value (a tab1 address or 64 hex
\ digits) at nval, or this wallet's id if none.
: nvalue
"'value':'" wtmp @ 80 lit jstr wtmp @ c@ 0= 0= and if
	wtmp @ strlen 3E lit = if wtmp @ wsd @ wkdec dup if wsd @ nval @ wkcan then
	else wtmp @ strlen 40 lit = dup if wtmp @ nval @ 20 lit jhexb then then
else waddr! wpk @ wsd @ wkid  wsd @ nval @ wkcan -1 lit then ;
\ wcfind ( -- flag )  the commit ncomc among the node's (/v1/commits): its
\ position at ncpos, its height ncht.
: wcfind
0 lit nfnd !  0 lit sfrom @ !  0 lit sfrom @ 4 lit + !
begin
	ppath @ "/v1/commits?from=" scpy  sfrom @ @ sfrom @ 4 lit + @ rot dstr "&count=1000" scpy 0 lit over c! drop
	ppath @ hget dup scur !  0 lit scnt !
	if
		begin scur @ "'position':" jfind ?dup while
			jnum scur !  nlo @ epos @ !  nhi @ epos @ 4 lit + !
			scur @ "'hash':'" jfind ecom @ 20 lit jhexb
			scur @ "'height':" jfind jnum scur !
			ecom @ ncomc @ 20 lit wssame if -1 lit nfnd !  epos @ ncpos @ 8 lit bcopy  nlo @ ncht ! then
			scnt @ 1 lit + scnt !
			epos @ @ 1 lit + dup sfrom @ !  0= if epos @ 4 lit + @ 1 lit + else epos @ 4 lit + @ then sfrom @ 4 lit + !
		repeat
	then
	scnt @ 3E8 lit u<  nfnd @ or
until
nfnd @ ;
\ nlook ( -- found ok )  the name nname looked up through the node, its
\ proof checked against the node's state root: found or not (its record:
\ owner at nlo... nrb's fields at ndone), ok 0 if the answer does not hold.
: nlok variable ;  : nlfnd variable ;  : nlown variable ;  : nlval variable ;  : nlmem variable ;
: nlook
0 lit nlok !  0 lit nlfnd !  wnpini
ppath @ "/v1/name/" scpy nname @ scpy 0 lit over c! drop
ppath @ hget ?dup if
	scur !
	nname @ nlen @ wnpk @ wnkey
	scur @ "'record':{" jfind ?dup if
		dup "'owner':'" jfind nlown @ 20 lit jhexb  dup "'value':'" jfind nlval @ 20 lit jhexb  "'memo':'" jfind nlmem @ 20 lit jhexb
		-1 lit nlfnd !
	then
	scur @ "'terminal':{" jfind ?dup if
		1 lit wnpt !  dup "'key':'" jfind wnptk @ 10 lit jhexb  "'value':'" jfind wtmp @ 20 lit jhexb  wtmp @ wnptv @ dle
	else 0 lit wnpt ! then
	0 lit wnpn !
	scur @ "'siblings':[" jfind ?dup if
		pcur !
		begin pcur @ c@ 5D lit <> pcur @ c@ and while
			pcur @ c@ 22 lit = if
				pcur @ 1 lit + wtmp @ 20 lit jhexb  wtmp @ wnps @ wnpn @ 5 lit lshift + dle  wnpn @ 1 lit + wnpn !
				pcur @ 42 lit + pcur !
			else pcur @ 1 lit + pcur ! then
		repeat
	then
	scur @ "'outputs_root':'" jfind wtmp @ 20 lit jhexb  wtmp @ wnpor @ dle
	scur @ "'state_root':'" jfind wtmp @ 20 lit jhexb  wtmp @ wnpsr @ dle
	nlfnd @ if
		nname @ nlen @ nlown @ nlval @ nlmem @ nrb @ wnrec nrl !  nrb @ wsd @ rvalue  wsd @ wnmem
	else wnabs then
	nlok !
then
nlfnd @ nlok @ ;

\ nadopt  after nlook found the name: an update pending whose new owner the
\ chain has is taken (its nonce and value the record's, a fresh key's
\ leaves); nownc the current owner's again.
: nadopt
nrecb @ 34 lit + c@ if
	nlown @ nownc @ 20 lit wssame 0= if
		nrecb @ 58 lit + nderive
		nlown @ nownc @ 20 lit wssame if
			nrecb @ 58 lit + nrecb @ 10 lit bcopy  nrecb @ 68 lit + nrecb @ 10 lit + 20 lit bcopy
			2 lit nrecb @ 30 lit + c!  4 lit 0 lit do 0 lit nrecb @ 31 lit + i + c! loop
			wbeg nmput wend drop
		then
		nrecb @ nderive
	then
then ;

\ oncommit ( line -- )  a name committed to (its value given, or this
\ wallet's id): a nonce, the commit and memo it makes, carried in a
\ transaction of the wallet's; the reveal may follow 12 blocks after.
: oncommit
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup nname? 0= if drop "not a valid name (1 to 32 of a-z, 0-9, _)" jerr else
nmget if drop "the wallet already has that name" jerr else
dup nvalue 0= if drop "a value is a tab1 address or 64 hex digits" jerr else
	wspeed
	nrecb @ NRECN 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
	4 lit 0 lit do nrecb @ i 2 lit lshift + wrfp loop
	nrecb @ nderive
	ncomc @ nmem @ nopb @ wncop wcon !  nopb @ wco !  0 lit wcx !  0 lit 0 lit samt @ a8set
	wcarry ?dup if wcerr else
		nval @ nrecb @ 10 lit + 20 lit bcopy  ncomc @ nrecb @ 38 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		wbeg nmput wend drop
		jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "','ready':12}" jo jend
	then
then then then then ;

\ onreveal ( line -- )  a committed name revealed: its commit found among
\ the node's, at least 12 blocks old; the record, the salt and the
\ commit's position carried.
: onreveal
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup nname? 0= if drop "not a valid name" jerr else
nmget 0= if drop "no commit to that name in this wallet" jerr else
nrecb @ 30 lit + c@ if drop "that name is revealed already" jerr else
	wspeed  wtick
	nrecb @ nderive
	wcfind 0= if "the commit is not in a block yet" jerr else
	lh @ ncht @ C lit + u< if "the commit is under 12 blocks old: reveal it later" jerr else
		nname @ nlen @ nownc @ nrecb @ 10 lit + nmem @ nrb @ wnrec drop
		nrb @ nsaltc @ ncpos @ nopb @ wnrop wcon !  nopb @ wco !  0 lit wcx !  0 lit 0 lit samt @ a8set
		wcarry ?dup if wcerr else
			1 lit nrecb @ 30 lit + c!  wbeg nmput wend drop
			jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
		then
	then then
then then then then ;

\ onupdate ( line -- )  an owned name's value changed: a record under a
\ fresh owner key (a new nonce, kept pending until the chain has it),
\ signed by the current owner's key at its next leaf (recorded used first).
: onupdate
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup nname? 0= if drop "not a valid name" jerr else
nmget 0= if drop "this wallet has no such name" jerr else
dup nvalue 0= if drop "a value is a tab1 address or 64 hex digits" jerr else
nrecb @ 32 lit + c@ 8 lit u< 0= if drop "its owner key has signed all it may" jerr else
	wspeed
	nrecb @ nderive
	nlook 0= if drop "the node does not answer for it" jerr else
	0= if "the name is not on chain" jerr else
	nadopt
	nlown @ nownc @ 20 lit wssame 0= if "the wallet is not its owner on chain" jerr else
		\ the leaf, recorded used before the signature
		nrecb @ 31 lit + c@ nrecb @ 32 lit + c@ + 7 lit and  nrecb @ 33 lit + c@ if 8 lit + then nmlv !
		2 lit nrecb @ 30 lit + c!  nrecb @ 32 lit + dup c@ 1 lit + swap c!
		4 lit 0 lit do nrecb @ 58 lit + i 2 lit lshift + wrfp loop  nval @ nrecb @ 68 lit + 20 lit bcopy  1 lit nrecb @ 34 lit + c!
		wbeg nmput wend 0= if "the wallet could not be written" jerr else
			\ the new record (the pending nonce's owner and memo), signed by the current key
			nrecb @ 58 lit + nderive
			nname @ nlen @ nownc @ nval @ nmem @ nrb @ wnrec drop
			nrecb @ nderive
			nrb @ nmlv @ nopb @ wnuop wcon !  nopb @ wco !  0 lit wcx !  0 lit 0 lit samt @ a8set
			wcarry ?dup if wcerr else
				jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
			then
		then
	then then then
then then then then then ;

\ onlook ( line -- )  a name looked up, checked against the state root.
: onlook
dup nname? 0= if drop "not a valid name" jerr else
drop nlook 0= if drop "the answer of the node does not hold" jerr else
	jok ",'found':" jo
	if
		"true,'owner':'" jo nlown @ 20 lit jhex "','value':'" jo nlval @ 20 lit jhex "'" jo
		nlval @ wsd @ dle  wsd @ waddr2 @ wkaddr  ",'address':'" jo waddr2 @ jraw "'" jo
	else "false" jo then
	"}" jo jend
then then ;

\ onames  the wallet's names: each its state (committed, ready, revealed,
\ owned; a pending update's new owner taken once the chain has it).
\ onoffer ( line -- )  a name asked for from its owner: a record under a
\ fresh key of this wallet's (its value given, or this wallet's id), kept
\ as offered (stage 3), given as text for the owner's name-transfer, or
\ written to the file in "file".  Asked again while offered, the same
\ offer again.
\ nofnew ( line -- code )  a new offer's record kept, the offer at nrb (nrl
\ bytes): 0, or 1 not a value, 2 not written.  nofold ( line -- 0 ) an
\ offered name's offer made again.
: ofile variable ;
: nofnew
nvalue 0= if 1 lit else
	nrecb @ NRECN 0 lit do 0 lit over i + c! loop drop
	4 lit 0 lit do nrecb @ i 2 lit lshift + wrfp loop
	nrecb @ nderive
	nname @ nlen @ nownc @ nval @ nmem @ nrb @ wnrec nrl !
	nval @ nrecb @ 10 lit + 20 lit bcopy  3 lit nrecb @ 30 lit + c!
	wbeg nmput wend 0= if 2 lit else 0 lit then
then ;
: nofold  drop  nrecb @ 10 lit + nval @ 20 lit bcopy  nrecb @ nderive  nname @ nlen @ nownc @ nval @ nmem @ nrb @ wnrec nrl !  0 lit ;
: onoffer
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup nname? 0= if drop "not a valid name" jerr else
dup "'file':'" fpath @ 100 lit jstr ofile !
nmget if nrecb @ 30 lit + c@ 3 lit = if nofold else drop 3 lit then else nofnew then
?dup if
	dup 1 lit = if drop "a value is a tab1 address or 64 hex digits" jerr else
	2 lit = if "the wallet could not be written" jerr else "the wallet already has that name" jerr then then
else
	ofile @ if
		boffer 0 lit bjs !  tout @ bbp !  nrb @ nrl @ b64out  bslate
		fpath @ tout @ bbp @ tout @ - fwrite if jok ",'file':'" jo fpath @ jraw "'}" jo jend else "the offer cannot be written" jerr then
	else boffer 1 lit bjs !  jok ",'text':'" jo nrb @ nrl @ b64out "'}" jo jend  0 lit bjs !  bslate then
then then then ;

\ nofb  the offer onxfer signs over (nlook takes nrb).
: nofb variable ;
\ tfile ( line -- line ok )  the request's text at ttxt: pasted ("text"),
\ or read from the file in "file".
: tfile
dup "'text':'" ttxt @ 2400 lit jstr if -1 lit else
dup "'file':'" fpath @ 100 lit jstr if
	fpath @ fread dup 0< over 23FF lit u> or if drop 0 lit else
		fbuf @ ttxt @ 2 lit pick bcopy  ttxt @ + 0 lit swap c!  -1 lit
	then
else 0 lit then then ;
\ onxfer ( line -- )  a name of this wallet's signed over to an offer
\ (pasted, "text", or a file's, "file"): an update to the offer's record by the current owner
\ key at its next leaf (recorded used first); the name leaves the wallet
\ when the chain has it (stage 4).
: onxfer
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
tfile 0= if drop "no offer given, or its file not read" jerr else
wspeed
boffer  ttxt @ nofb @ b64in  bslate  dup 0< if drop "no name offer in it" jerr else
nrl !  nofb @ c@ dup nlen !  1 lit - 20 lit u< 0= if "not a name offer" jerr else
nofb @ 1 lit + nname @ nlen @ bcopy  0 lit nname @ nlen @ + c!
nmget 0= if "this wallet has no such name" jerr else
nrecb @ 32 lit + c@ 8 lit u< 0= if "its owner key has signed all it may" jerr else
	nrecb @ nderive
	nlook 0= if drop "the node does not answer for it" jerr else
	0= if "the name is not on chain" jerr else
	nadopt
	nlown @ nownc @ 20 lit wssame 0= if "the wallet is not its owner on chain" jerr else
		nrecb @ 31 lit + c@ nrecb @ 32 lit + c@ + 7 lit and  nrecb @ 33 lit + c@ if 8 lit + then nmlv !
		nrecb @ 32 lit + dup c@ 1 lit + swap c!  4 lit nrecb @ 30 lit + c!
		wbeg nmput wend 0= if "the wallet could not be written" jerr else
			nrecb @ nderive
			nofb @ nmlv @ nopb @ wnuop wcon !  nopb @ wco !  0 lit wcx !  0 lit 0 lit samt @ a8set
			wcarry ?dup if wcerr else
				jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "','name':'" jo nname @ jraw "'}" jo jend
			then
		then
	then then then
then then then then then then ;

: nanm variable ;  : nkl variable ;  : ntx variable ;
: onames
have @ 0= if nowal else
	wtick
	jok ",'items':[" jo  0 lit nanm !
	6E lit okey @ c!  1 lit nkl !
	begin
		wfd @ 0 lit txbegin ntx !  ntx @ okey @ nkl @ okn @ txnext  ntx @ txabort drop
		dup 1 lit u> if okn @ c@ 6E lit = else 0 lit then  nanm @ 10 lit u< and
	while
		dup nkl !  1 lit - nlen !
		okn @ 1 lit + nname @ nlen @ bcopy  0 lit nname @ nlen @ + c!
		okn @ okey @ nkl @ bcopy
		nmget drop
		nanm @ if "," jo then  nanm @ 1 lit + nanm !
		"{'name':'" jo nname @ jraw "','value':'" jo nrecb @ 10 lit + 20 lit jhex "','state':'" jo
		nrecb @ 30 lit + c@ 0= if
			nrecb @ nderive
			wcfind if
				lh @ ncht @ C lit + u< if "committed','ready':" jo ncht @ C lit + lh @ - 0 lit wdec else "ready','ready':0" jo then
			else "committed','ready':12" jo then
		else
			nrecb @ nderive  nlook drop if
				nadopt
				nlown @ nownc @ 20 lit wssame if "owned" else
				nrecb @ 30 lit + c@ 3 lit = if "offered" else nrecb @ 30 lit + c@ 4 lit = if "transferred" else "revealed" then then then jo
			else nrecb @ 30 lit + c@ 3 lit = if "offered" else "revealed" then jo then
			"','ready':0" jo
		then
		"}" jo
	repeat drop
	"]}" jo jend
then ;

\ hexs ( a n dst -- )  n bytes in hex, a string at dst.
: hxd  F lit and dup A lit u< if 30 lit + else 57 lit + then ;
: hexs
swap ?dup if 0 lit do over i + c@ dup 4 lit rshift hxd 2 lit pick c!  hxd over 1 lit + c!  2 lit + loop then
0 lit swap c!  drop ;
\ oact  the activity: payments sent (by their id; pending until the scan
\ finds their output in the set), outputs received (by their commitment;
\ change left out, spent ones marked).
: anum variable ;
: oact
have @ 0= if nowal else
	jok ",'items':[" jo  0 lit anum !
	wfd @ 0 lit txbegin wtx !
	70 lit okey @ c!  1 lit
	begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 70 lit = else 0 lit then  anum @ 10 lit u< and while
		drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wgetk drop
		anum @ if "," jo then  anum @ 1 lit + anum !
		"{'tx':'" jo okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit jhex "','kind':'sent','amount':'" jo prec @ a8. "','state':'" jo
		prec @ 98 lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit = if "pending','height':0}" jo else "confirmed','height':" jo prec @ 9C lit + @ 0 lit wdec "}" jo then
		21 lit
	repeat drop
	6F lit okey @ c!  1 lit
	begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 6F lit = else 0 lit then  anum @ 10 lit u< and while
		drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
		orec @ 2C lit + c@ 2 lit <> if
			anum @ if "," jo then  anum @ 1 lit + anum !
			"{'tx':'" jo okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit jhex "','kind':'received','amount':'" jo orec @ 10 lit + a8.
			"','state':'" jo orec @ 24 lit + c@ 2 lit = if "spent" else orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit = if "pending" else "confirmed" then then jo
			"','height':" jo orec @ 20 lit + @ 0 lit wdec "}" jo
		then
		21 lit
	repeat drop
	wtx @ txabort drop
	"]}" jo jend
then ;

\ wsums  the balance in tabminer's five sums (wallet.rs's Balance), 8
\ bytes each: sa1 confirmed (unspent, in the set), sa2 pending (unspent,
\ not yet in it: change, rewards), sa4 unverified (an output added to
\ another's slate, not yet in the set), sa3 reserved (picked for a slate,
\ not signed), sa5 locked (signed away, still in the set).
: sa1 variable ;  : sa2 variable ;  : sa3 variable ;  : sa4 variable ;  : sa5 variable ;  : sacc variable ;
: a8z  0 lit over !  0 lit swap 4 lit + ! ;               \ ( a -- )
: wsums
sa1 @ a8z  sa2 @ a8z  sa3 @ a8z  sa4 @ a8z  sa5 @ a8z
wfd @ 0 lit txbegin wtx !
6F lit okey @ c!  1 lit
begin wtx @ okey @ rot okn @ txnext dup 21 lit = if okn @ c@ 6F lit = else 0 lit then while
	drop  okn @ okey @ 21 lit bcopy
	okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop
	0 lit sacc !
	orec @ 24 lit + c@ dup 0= if
		drop orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <> if sa1 else orec @ 2C lit + c@ 1 lit = if sa4 else sa2 then then @ sacc !
	else 1 lit = if sa3 @ sacc ! else
		orec @ 1C lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <>  orec @ 28 lit + @ sgen @ = and if sa5 @ sacc ! then
	then then
	sacc @ if orec @ 10 lit + sacc @ sacc @ a8add then
	21 lit
repeat drop
wtx @ txabort drop ;

\ Cancel and bump (as tabminer's cancel_sent and bump_sent, docs/FEES.md):
\ a payment or burn not yet in a block, re-signed from the same inputs at
\ their next leaves.  A replacement pays what it replaces and 10 base
\ units a byte of its own size more (the pool's rule), or the speed's
\ rate on its size if more.
\ xload ( line -- code )  the transaction in "tx" (its id at xid): 0 and
\ its records at prec and xrec, or why not.
: xload
"'tx':'" wtmp @ 50 lit jstr  wtmp @ strlen 40 lit = and 0= if 1 lit else
wtmp @ xid @ 20 lit jhexb
70 lit okey @ c!  xid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wrget 0< if 2 lit else
prec @ 98 lit + @ FFFFFFFF lit <> if 3 lit else
78 lit okey @ c!  okey @ 21 lit xrec @ 400 lit wrget 0< if 4 lit else 0 lit
then then then then ;
: xerr
dup 1 lit = if drop "no transaction id" jerr else dup 2 lit = if drop "no payment or burn with that id" jerr else
3 lit = if "it is in a block already" jerr else "the wallet kept no record of its inputs (sent before cancel and bump were built)" jerr then
then then ;
\ xfee ( base -- )  sfee = the larger of base + 10 a byte of xsz and
\ srate a byte of xsz.
: xfee
xsz @ A lit * 0 lit wtmp @ a8set  wtmp @ sfee @ a8add
xsz @ srate @ * 0 lit wtmp @ a8set  sfee @ wtmp @ a8lt if wtmp @ sfee @ 8 lit bcopy then ;
\ xins  a transaction begun (wcbeg) with the record's inputs, their sum at
\ stot; wib, wist, win for winp.
: xins
wcbeg  0 lit 0 lit stot @ a8set
xrec @ @ 0 lit do
	xrec @ 38 lit + i 5 lit lshift + pkb @ wpkof
	stot @ orec @ 10 lit + stot @ a8add  pkb @ orec @ 10 lit + wcin+
loop
xrec @ 38 lit + wib !  20 lit wist !  xrec @ @ win ! ;
\ xpost ( -- code )  the transaction signed (its leaves recorded first)
\ and posted: wcarry's codes (0 done, its id at ecb; 3, 4, 5, 6).
: xpost
winp if 3 lit else
wleaf+ 0= if 4 lit else
	fka @ flv @ fps @ wctx ftx !
	"POST" "/v1/tx" wctb @ ftx @ hask
	hcode @ C8 lit = if drop  wsd @ wcbody  wsd @ ecb @ wkcan  0 lit
	else ?dup if "'reason':'" wcwhy @ 100 lit jstr drop wcwhy @ jsafe 5 lit else 6 lit then then
then then ;
\ xforget ( c -- )  an output made for a replacement that was not sent.
: xforget  wbeg  6F lit okey @ c!  okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop  wend drop ;
\ xdrop  in the writer's transaction: the replaced transaction's sent
\ record and its change's output record (it will not land).
: xdrop
78 lit okey @ c!  xid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop
xrec @ 4 lit + @ if 6F lit okey @ c!  xrec @ 18 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop then ;
\ ocancel ( line -- )  "tx" replaced by its inputs paid back to a new
\ output of this wallet's: the payment (or burn) and its records go.
: ocancel
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup xload ?dup if nip xerr else
	wspeed
	xrec @ @ 949 lit * 4C lit + xsz !  xrec @ 8 lit + xfee
	xins
	sfee @ stot @ a8lt 0= if "its inputs hold too little for that fee" jerr else
	stot @ sfee @ schg @ a8sub
	schg @ sdust @ a8lt if "what would come back is below the dust limit" jerr else
	wbeg  schg @ 2 lit wnew  wend 0= if "the wallet could not be written" jerr else
		ecom @ xout @ 20 lit bcopy  onew @ wcout+
		xpost ?dup if xout @ xforget wcerr else
			wbeg
			70 lit okey @ c!  xid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop
			6 lit 0 lit do i rpkey  wtx @ okey @ 22 lit txdel drop loop
			xdrop
			wend drop
			jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
		then
	then then then
then then ;
\ obump ( line -- )  "tx" replaced by the same outputs but its change,
\ which pays the higher fee (below the dust limit, the change goes to the
\ fee whole): the payment's records move to the replacement.
: bchg2 variable ;
: obump
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
dup xload ?dup if nip xerr else
xrec @ 4 lit + @ 0= if drop "it has no change to pay a higher fee from: cancel it instead" jerr else
	wspeed
	xrec @ 10 lit + @ xsz !  xrec @ 8 lit + xfee
	sfee @ xrec @ 8 lit + samt @ a8sub
	xins
	6F lit okey @ c!  xrec @ 18 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wrget drop
	orec @ 10 lit + stot @ 8 lit bcopy
	stot @ samt @ a8lt if "its change holds too little for that fee: cancel it instead" jerr else
	stot @ samt @ schg @ a8sub  0 lit bchg2 !  -1 lit fcode !
	schg @ sdust @ a8lt if
		xrec @ 8 lit + stot @ sfee @ a8add
	else
		wbeg  schg @ 2 lit wnew  wend 0= if 0 lit fcode ! else ecom @ xout @ 20 lit bcopy  onew @ wcout+  1 lit bchg2 ! then
	then
	fcode @ 0= if "the wallet could not be written" jerr else
		prec @ A0 lit + xout @ 20 lit + 3C lit bcopy  xout @ 20 lit + wcout+
		xpost ?dup if bchg2 @ if xout @ xforget then wcerr else
			wbeg
			\ the payment's record and its receipt's parts, moved to the new id
			sfee @ prec @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy
			70 lit okey @ c!  ecb @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit prec @ PRECN wsetk
			xid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop
			6 lit 0 lit do
				xid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  i rpkey  okey @ 22 lit pftxt @ RPART wgetk
				dup 0 lit > if
					wtx @ okey @ 22 lit txdel drop
					ecb @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  i rpkey  okey @ 22 lit rot pftxt @ swap wsetk
				else drop then
			loop
			xdrop
			\ its own sent record: the same inputs, the new change
			bchg2 @ xrec @ 4 lit + !  sfee @ xrec @ 8 lit + 8 lit bcopy  ftx @ xrec @ 10 lit + !
			xout @ xrec @ 18 lit + 20 lit bcopy  xrec @ 38 lit + xsrc !  20 lit xst !  xrec @ @ wxput
			wend drop
			jok ",'tx':'" jo ecb @ 20 lit jhex "','fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
		then
	then then
then then then ;

\ ── The message layer (phase 3, docs/ONION.md, init mode): payments by
\ address or name with no file.  Started once the wallet is open
\ (wmstart): its seeds (/etc/wallet/config: "seed HOST:PORT" lines, or
\ "messages off"; none, tabminer's), its identity (the address's Dilithium key), a
\ session at each of its rendezvous points (node/wnet.fam).  A payment
\ sent online (send-online) goes as a slate in a payload to the
\ recipient's id, its answer finalized when it comes from that id; a
\ payer's slate that comes is answered at once.  What happens is told as
\ events: {"event":"message","text":...}, a finalized payment as the
\ finalize request's answer with "event":"message" in place of the id. ──
: wmtried variable ;  : wmoff variable ;  : wonline variable ;  : wmsd variable ;  : wmsn variable ;  : wmto variable ;  : wmsid variable ;  : wmkind variable ;
: wmst0 variable ;  : wmlast variable ;  : wmx variable ;  : wmy variable ;
\ wmscmp ( a b -- flag )  string a sorts before b (as bytes).
: wmscmp
begin over c@ over c@ = over c@ and while 1 lit + swap 1 lit + swap repeat
c@ swap c@ swap u< ;
\ wmadd ( s -- )  a seed (HOST:PORT) kept, in order, once.
: wmadd
wmsn @ 8 lit u< if
	wmx !  0 lit wmy !
	wmsn @ ?dup if 0 lit do wmsd @ i 6 lit lshift + wmx @ streq if -1 lit wmy ! then loop then
	wmy @ 0= if
		\ the place: after those before it
		0 lit wmsn @ ?dup if 0 lit do wmsd @ i 6 lit lshift + wmx @ wmscmp if drop i 1 lit + then loop then
		dup wmsn @ swap - ?dup if 0 lit do
			wmsd @ wmsn @ i - 1 lit - 6 lit lshift +  dup 40 lit + 40 lit bcopy
		loop then
		wmsd @ swap 6 lit lshift + wmx @ scpy 0 lit swap c!
		wmsn @ 1 lit + wmsn !
	then
then ;
\ wmdots ( s -- ip ok )  a dotted IPv4 address (to a ':' or NUL).
: wmdots
0 lit swap  -1 lit wmy !
4 lit 0 lit do
	0 lit wmx !  dup c@ 30 lit - A lit u< 0= if 0 lit wmy ! then
	begin dup c@ 30 lit - A lit u< while dup c@ 30 lit - wmx @ A lit * + wmx !  1 lit + repeat
	swap 8 lit lshift wmx @ FF lit and or swap
	i 3 lit < if dup c@ 2E lit = if 1 lit + else 0 lit wmy ! then then
loop
drop wmy @ ;
\ wmseeds  /etc/wallet/config's "seed HOST:PORT" lines, else tabminer's
\ seeds; sorted; each looked up (dns.fam, at QEMU's resolver) and added.
\ A line "messages off": none (wmoff).
: wmseeds
0 lit wmsn !  0 lit wmoff !
"/etc/wallet/config" fread dup 0< if drop else
	0 lit swap fbuf @ + c!  fbuf @
	begin dup c@ while
		dup "messages off" C lit dlsame if -1 lit wmoff ! then
		dup "seed " 5 lit dlsame if
			5 lit + dup wtmp @ swap
			begin dup c@ dup 20 lit u> swap 7F lit u< and while 2dup c@ swap c! swap 1 lit + swap 1 lit + repeat
			drop 0 lit swap c!  wtmp @ wmadd
		then
		begin dup c@ dup 0= 0= swap A lit <> and while 1 lit + repeat
		dup c@ if 1 lit + then
	repeat drop
then
wmsn @ 0= wmoff @ 0= and if "tabernacle1.root.sx:3737" wmadd  "tabernacle2.root.sx:3737" wmadd then
dinit
wmsn @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	wmsd @ i 6 lit lshift + wtmp @ swap scpy 0 lit swap c!
	wtmp @ begin dup c@ dup 0= 0= swap 3A lit <> and while 1 lit + repeat
	dup c@ if 0 lit over c! 1 lit + atoi else drop E99 lit then
	wtmp @ wmdots 0= if drop wtmp @ A000203 lit 35 lit dlook then
	swap mnseed
loop then ;
\ wmstart  the message layer begun: seeds, identity, the genesis's id.
: wmstart
-1 lit wmtried !
mninit  wmseeds
wmoff @ 0= if -1 lit wonline !  waddr!  wpk @ wsk @ mnkeys then
"/v1/header/0" hget ?dup if "'id':'" jfind ?dup if mngen @ 20 lit jhexb then then
mnms wmlast ! ;
\ wmev ( s -- )  an event telling s.
: wmev  "{'event':'message','text':'" jo jo "'}" jo jend ;
\ wmidb ( s -- )  idb = s, each ' a double quote (jraw writes idb as it is).
: wmidb  idb @ swap begin dup c@ while dup c@ dup 27 lit = if drop 22 lit then 2 lit pick c!  1 lit + swap 1 lit + swap repeat drop 0 lit swap c! ;
\ wmcanc  the slate at wmsid abandoned (its send failed): its inputs free
\ again, its change forgotten, its records gone.
: wmcanc
73 lit okey @ c!  wmsid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
okey @ 21 lit pend @ 878 lit wrget 0< 0= if
	wbeg
	pend @ @ ?dup if 0 lit do
		6F lit okey @ c!  pend @ 78 lit + i 5 lit lshift + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
		okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wgetk drop  0 lit orec @ 24 lit + c!  okey @ 21 lit orec @ 30 lit wsetk
	loop then
	pend @ 4 lit + @ if 6F lit okey @ c!  pend @ 58 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop then
	73 lit okey @ c!  wmsid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop
	74 lit okey @ c!  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop
	wend drop
then ;
\ wmto! ( s -- ok )  wmto = the id of s: a tab1 address, 64 hex digits,
\ or @NAME (its value on chain, looked up through the node, its proof
\ checked).
: wmto!
dup c@ 40 lit = if
	1 lit + nname @ swap scpy 0 lit swap c!  nname @ strlen dup nlen !  nname @ swap wnok if
		nlook if if nlval @ wmto @ 20 lit bcopy  0 lit  20 lit 0 lit do wmto @ i + c@ or loop 0= 0= else 0 lit then else 0 lit then
	else 0 lit then
else dup strlen 3E lit = if wsd @ wkdec dup if wsd @ wmto @ wkcan then
else dup strlen 40 lit = if wmto @ 20 lit jhexb -1 lit else drop 0 lit then then then ;
\ osonl ( line -- )  a payment sent online: "to" (an address or @NAME),
\ "amount", "speed"; the slate made (as osend's), sent to the
\ recipient's id; its answer finalized when it comes.
: osonl
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
wonline @ 0= if drop "the message layer is not started" jerr else
mnlive 0= if drop "not reachable yet: no rendezvous point holds a session for this wallet" jerr else
mnss @ if drop "a message is under way; try again in a moment" jerr else
dup "'to':'" wtmp @ 80 lit jstr 0= if drop "no recipient given" jerr else
wtmp @ wmto! 0= if drop "not an address, nor a registered name" jerr else
	-1 lit wmon !  0 lit wmok !  osend  0 lit wmon !
	wmok @ if
		sid @ wmsid @ 20 lit bcopy  1 lit wmkind !
		wbeg  74 lit okey @ c!  sid @ okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  okey @ 21 lit wmto @ 20 lit wsetk  wend drop
		wmto @ 1 lit wsbuf @ fpn @ mnsend drop
		jok ",'online':true,'fee':'" jo sfee @ a8. "'}" jo jend
	then
then then then then then then ;
\ wmgot  a payload opened: a slate.  A payer's (stage 1) answered and
\ sent back to it; a recipient's answer (stage 2) to a payment this
\ wallet sent that id, finalized.
: wmgot
mgkind @ 1 lit =  mgil @ 8000 lit u< and if
	mgin @ sbin @ mgil @ bcopy  mgil @ fpn !
	sbin @ fpn @ wsparse if
		wsstg @ 1 lit =  wsnout @ wschg @ = and  mnss @ 0= and if
			waddr!
			wbeg  wsa @ 49 lit + 1 lit wnew  wend if
				onew @ wsk @ wpk @ wsans fpn !
				2 lit wmkind !  mgfrom @ 1 lit wsbuf @ fpn @ mnsendr drop
				"{'event':'message','text':'answered a slate of " jo wsa @ 49 lit + a8. " coins from a payer; it is paid once the payer sends it'}" jo jend
			then
		then
		wsstg @ 2 lit = if
			74 lit okey @ c!  wsa @ 8 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy
			okey @ 21 lit wtmp @ 20 lit wrget 20 lit =  wtmp @ mgfrom @ 20 lit dlsame and if
				"null,'event':'message'" wmidb  ofinb  "null" wmidb
				wbeg  74 lit okey @ c!  wsa @ 8 lit + okey @ 1 lit + 20 lit bcopy  wtx @ okey @ 21 lit txdel drop  wend drop
			then
		then
	then
then ;
\ wmrun  the message layer's turn in the loop: datagrams, the clock, the
\ height and tip from the node, the send's end told.
: wmrun
mnin  mnrcv @ if wmgot then
lh @ mnht !  ntip @ c@ if ntip @ mntip @ 20 lit jhexb then
mntick
mnst @ if
	mnst @ 1 lit = if
		wmkind @ 1 lit = if "the slate reached a rendezvous point of the recipient; waiting for the answer" wmev then
	else
		wmkind @ 1 lit = if wmcanc then
		wtmp @ "the message was not delivered: " scpy mnwhy @ scpy 0 lit over c! drop  wtmp @ jsafe wtmp @ wmev
	then
	0 lit mnst !
then ;

\ ── The requests ──

: tried variable ;
: oview
wtick  wsums
jok ",'confirmed':'" jo sa1 @ wsum.  "','pending':'" jo sa2 @ wsum.  "','unverified':'" jo sa4 @ wsum.  "','reserved':'" jo sa3 @ wsum.
"','locked':'" jo sa5 @ wsum.  "','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec  ",'node':'" jo nodeok @ if "synced" else "not reached" then jo
"','reach':" jo wonline @ if mnlive else 0 lit then 0 lit wdec  "}" jo jend ;
\ oscan  the whole set scanned again now; the tip and the scan told.
: oscan
have @ 0= if nowal else
	jok "}" jo jend
	0 lit ltip @ c!  wtick
	"{'event':'scan','height':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec ",'of':" jo lh @ 0 lit wdec "}" jo jend
then ;
: ocreate
have @ if "there is a wallet already" jerr else
	plain @ 10 lit wrand  plain @ wphr @ b39phr  wphr @ "" plain @ 10 lit + b39seed drop
	0 lit wmake if jok ",'words':'" jo wphr @ jraw "'}" jo jend  wtick else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
then ;
: orestore
have @ if drop "there is a wallet already" jerr else
	dup "'words':'" wphr @ 100 lit jstr 0= if drop "no words" jerr else
		"'passphrase':'" wtmp @ 100 lit jstr drop
		wphr @ wtmp @ plain @ 10 lit + b39seed
		dup 0= if
			drop  wphr @ plain @ b39ent drop
			1 lit wmake if jok "}" jo jend  wtick else "the wallet could not be written" jerr then
		else
			dup FFFFFFFF lit = if drop "a phrase is 12 words" jerr else
			FFFFFFFE lit = if "a word is not in the list" jerr else
			"the checksum of the words does not match: a word is wrong" jerr then then
		then
	then
then ;
: ophrase
have @ 0= if drop nowal else
	"'password':'" wtmp @ 100 lit jstr 0= if "no password" jerr else
		wtmp @ wunseal if
			plain @ wphr @ b39phr  jok ",'words':'" jo wphr @ jraw "'}" jo jend
		else "not the password" jerr then
	then
then ;
: oreceive
have @ 0= if nowal else waddr!  jok ",'address':'" jo waddr @ jraw "'}" jo jend then ;

\ unlk ( line -- )  the first line: wm's, the session's password.
: unlk
"unlock" op? if
	"'password':'" pw @ 100 lit jstr pw @ c@ 0= 0= and if
		0 lit wopen if
			"secret" rec @ 100 lit wget 0< if
				1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':false}" jo jend
			else
				pw @ wunseal if
					wload  1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':true}" jo jend  wtick
				else "{'op':'unlock','ok':false,'error':'the wallet is sealed under another password than the session'}" jo jend then
			then
		else 1 lit unl !  "{'op':'unlock','ok':true,'wallet':false}" jo jend then
	else "{'op':'unlock','ok':false,'error':'no password'}" jo jend then
else drop "locked" jerr then ;

\ answer ( line -- )  a request answered by its op.
: answer
"overview" op? if drop have @ if oview else nowal then else
"receive" op? if drop oreceive else
"create" op? if drop ocreate else
"restore" op? if orestore else
"phrase" op? if ophrase else
"unlock" op? if drop "unlocked already" jerr else
"scan" op? if drop oscan else
"fees" op? if drop ofees else
"answer" op? if oanswer else
"send" op? if osend else
"finalize" op? if ofinal else
"activity" op? if drop oact else
"proof" op? if oproof else
"verify" op? if overify else
"burn" op? if oburn else
"names" op? if drop onames else
"name-commit" op? if oncommit else
"name-reveal" op? if onreveal else
"name-update" op? if onupdate else
"name-lookup" op? if onlook else
"name-offer" op? if onoffer else
"name-transfer" op? if onxfer else
"send-online" op? if osonl else
"cancel" op? if ocancel else
"bump" op? if obump else
drop "unknown op" jerr
then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then ;

\ hline ( line -- )  a line read: only the first may unlock.
: hline
dup getid  dup getop
unl @ if answer else tried @ if drop "locked" jerr else 1 lit tried ! unlk then then ;

\ lines  each whole line read handled; the rest, a line begun, kept.
: lines
0 lit lp !
begin
	lp @ le !
	begin le @ icnt @ u<  ibuf @ le @ + c@ A lit <> and while le @ 1 lit + le ! repeat
	le @ icnt @ u<
while
	0 lit ibuf @ le @ + c!  ibuf @ lp @ + hline
	le @ 1 lit + lp !
repeat
icnt @ lp @ - dup if dup 0 lit do ibuf @ lp @ + i + c@ ibuf @ i + c! loop then
icnt ! ;

wsinit  b39load drop  xkinit  wpinit  wninit  bslate
